WEBVTT

1
00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:04.397
<i>Go off!</i>

2
00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:07.317
<i>Block it!</i>

3
00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:08.360
<i>Block it!</i>

4
00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:09.236
<i>Dodge!</i>

5
00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:12.155
<i>Dodge! Move!</i>

6
00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:14.408
<i>One, two...</i>

7
00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:15.909
<i>One, two, three...</i>

8
00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:17.661
<i>Go on!</i>

9
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:20.289
One, two, three...

10
00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.082
One, two, three...

11
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:24.918
Sequence, go!

12
00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:27.337
Again!

13
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.799
Elbow.

14
00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:32.593
Elbow.

15
00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.594
Higher.

16
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.512
Higher. Elbow.

17
00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.892
Move, you've been on it for an hour!

18
00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:42.269
- You talking to me, motherfucker?
- Fuck off!

19
00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:43.896
Son of a bitch!

20
00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:20.224
You did well staying out of it earlier.

21
00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:24.895
I tried to escape once.
I got another 45 days.

22
00:02:25.062 --> 00:02:26.730
I ended up in Cell 7,

23
00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:29.733
up in Fresnes' fourth section.

24
00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:32.778
I was pacing around my cell.

25
00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:35.489
I'd been in the hole 3 or 4 days.

26
00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:38.033
Suddenly, I saw bubbles in the john.

27
00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:42.162
I walked over
and saw the snout of a rat,

28
00:02:42.496 --> 00:02:43.580
crawling out.

29
00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.918
I fed it. And I tamed it.

30
00:02:48.836 --> 00:02:50.879
I had conversations with a rat.

31
00:02:51.046 --> 00:02:52.130
A rat!

32
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.260
That's solitude and emptiness.

33
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.684
<i>There's nothing, no more humanity.</i>

34
00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:06.061
<i>Nothing but oblivion.</i>

35
00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:10.440
<i>The void.</i>

36
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.071
<i>There's no more love.
There's nothing.</i>

37
00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:20.742
<i>You don't belong anywhere.</i>

38
00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:23.328
<i>You're not wanted.</i>

39
00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:30.627
<i>Being forgotten is the worst part.</i>

40
00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.258
<i>We're the forgotten.</i>

41
00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:44.766
<i>You're alone with the wall people.</i>

42
00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.646
<i>They're there, watching you.</i>

43
00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:51.982
<i>They're all dead.</i>

44
00:03:54.151 --> 00:03:55.360
<i>You have to resist.</i>

45
00:03:57.654 --> 00:03:59.740
<i>It's not too late for you.</i>

46
00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:08.165
Mr. Darba,
you've been granted day parole.

47
00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:10.709
You'll have certain obligations.

48
00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:13.629
You must respect them.
It's important for next steps.

49
00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.714
Good, thank you.

50
00:04:15.881 --> 00:04:17.257
Hold onto this document.

51
00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.302
It proves
you left the facility legally.

52
00:04:20.469 --> 00:04:24.598
Your attendance certificate
lists your periods of incarceration.

53
00:04:24.765 --> 00:04:26.016
Any questions?

54
00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:29.478
Great. You may go.

55
00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:31.313
Good luck for the future.

56
00:05:13.063 --> 00:05:14.314
Samir Darba!

57
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.651
Hey, Samir!

58
00:05:19.486 --> 00:05:20.946
I'm talking to you.

59
00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:23.657
What?

60
00:05:23.824 --> 00:05:26.451
- Farhat wants you to move this.
- I don't work for him.

61
00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:29.121
Says who? Where are you going?

62
00:05:29.413 --> 00:05:30.414
You don't get it.

63
00:05:30.873 --> 00:05:32.207
No, you don't get it.

64
00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:33.917
Tell Farhat to go fuck himself.

65
00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:37.129
Farhat's gonna fuck you, bitch!

66
00:05:45.304 --> 00:05:47.890
The sentencing judge doesn't like you.

67
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.685
He's pretty intolerant
when it comes to drugs.

68
00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:02.529
I know your file well,
and I know what you've been through.

69
00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:04.865
You can show the judge he's wrong.

70
00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:06.033
Okay?

71
00:06:07.034 --> 00:06:09.995
To do that,
make sure tomorrow goes very well.

72
00:06:11.288 --> 00:06:12.539
You understand why?

73
00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:14.917
Yes?

74
00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:19.505
I spoke to Mr. Vasseur.

75
00:06:19.755 --> 00:06:22.174
He's very clear.
If your trial day goes well,

76
00:06:23.008 --> 00:06:24.259
he'll offer you the job.

77
00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:27.679
This is the construction site.

78
00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:31.475
This is where you're sleeping tonight.

79
00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:34.102
It's a new one.
A bit further away.

80
00:06:34.311 --> 00:06:37.439
These are the papers they'll ask for.

81
00:07:09.263 --> 00:07:11.139
One, two… Three!

82
00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.059
That's what your mother said?

83
00:07:14.852 --> 00:07:17.437
- Why?
- She has no money.

84
00:07:17.646 --> 00:07:19.189
What else could she say?

85
00:07:21.149 --> 00:07:22.484
What did you do?

86
00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:25.153
- Your leg's better.
- What?

87
00:07:26.321 --> 00:07:27.489
Your leg seems better.

88
00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:30.951
The doctor said it's not broken.

89
00:07:31.368 --> 00:07:33.161
Thanks for your help back there.

90
00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:37.958
- Where are you from?
- Senegal.

91
00:07:39.042 --> 00:07:40.627
- Senegal?
- Yeah.

92
00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:42.504
You seem okay here.

93
00:07:42.671 --> 00:07:44.590
Praise be to God, I can't complain.

94
00:07:45.174 --> 00:07:48.135
I came here because it was even worse
in my country.

95
00:07:48.302 --> 00:07:49.845
God gave me a second chance.

96
00:07:50.012 --> 00:07:52.639
Every day, I praise God.

97
00:07:58.604 --> 00:08:00.189
Have a good evening, guys.

98
00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:04.568
So?

99
00:08:05.402 --> 00:08:07.487
The day wasn't too tough on you?

100
00:08:08.155 --> 00:08:09.448
You did good work.

101
00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:12.618
Would you like to join the team?

102
00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.495
I can offer you a full-time contract.

103
00:08:15.662 --> 00:08:19.166
I'll call your advisor
and sort the paperwork.

104
00:08:19.333 --> 00:08:21.376
Come find me when you're released.

105
00:08:22.211 --> 00:08:23.045
Thank you.

106
00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:42.940
Samir!

107
00:08:44.358 --> 00:08:45.484
You little bitch!

108
00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.821
You got fucked so much in jail
that you've gone deaf!

109
00:08:51.323 --> 00:08:53.367
Stop ignoring me, bitch!

110
00:08:55.202 --> 00:08:56.286
I'm talking to you.

111
00:08:57.246 --> 00:08:57.996
Come here!

112
00:08:58.163 --> 00:09:00.582
Go around the block!
Go! Go!

113
00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:02.167
Move!

114
00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.094
Let me off!

115
00:12:44.264 --> 00:12:46.934
- That was good.
- Lots of fish.

116
00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.979
Sam! Hi, Sam!

117
00:13:34.606 --> 00:13:35.774
How's my girl?

118
00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:38.819
Hurry up, I'm starving!

119
00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:41.321
Who do you think this is for?

120
00:13:41.572 --> 00:13:44.783
Will you take me to school
this morning?

121
00:13:45.158 --> 00:13:46.785
Only if you give me a kiss.

122
00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.043
Let's take a ride on the motorbike.

123
00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.629
Yeah! Motorbike!

124
00:14:16.815 --> 00:14:17.691
You okay?

125
00:14:18.984 --> 00:14:20.027
Slept well?

126
00:14:20.652 --> 00:14:21.528
Not really.

127
00:14:21.695 --> 00:14:22.821
And the baby?

128
00:14:23.405 --> 00:14:25.073
He's been moving all night long.

129
00:14:29.661 --> 00:14:30.913
What are you doing?

130
00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:33.415
There are people
in Mommy’s restaurant.

131
00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:37.544
Sam, Mia, Dara and the baby.

132
00:14:37.711 --> 00:14:39.213
Put them in the restaurant.

133
00:14:39.671 --> 00:14:41.131
Let's eat in the kitchen.

134
00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:42.299
Here, honey.

135
00:14:44.218 --> 00:14:44.885
Repeat.

136
00:14:45.719 --> 00:14:46.637
Enjoy your meal.

137
00:14:46.803 --> 00:14:47.721
Enjoy your meal.

138
00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.099
Here.

139
00:15:02.361 --> 00:15:03.612
Give Mommy a kiss!

140
00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:05.989
Work hard today.

141
00:15:06.365 --> 00:15:08.325
Love you, Mommy!
Bye, Sam!

142
00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:17.918
Off you go!

143
00:15:27.719 --> 00:15:28.720
See you tonight.

144
00:15:49.616 --> 00:15:51.702
Your badge, please.

145
00:15:59.251 --> 00:15:59.960
You can go.

146
00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:22.274
Dusit Hotel?

147
00:16:26.612 --> 00:16:27.571
You're French?

148
00:16:27.738 --> 00:16:29.198
Wait over here.

149
00:16:57.267 --> 00:16:58.018
Sombat!

150
00:16:59.269 --> 00:17:00.187
Sombat!

151
00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.824
My head hurts.
Got any aspirin?

152
00:17:22.709 --> 00:17:23.417
Thanks.

153
00:17:25.838 --> 00:17:27.631
Did you play again last night?

154
00:17:28.924 --> 00:17:30.759
I'll get it back tonight.

155
00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:32.761
Don't worry.

156
00:17:34.054 --> 00:17:36.557
I'll help you a little
if I win too much.

157
00:17:40.018 --> 00:17:41.854
Are you going to watch Sam's fight?

158
00:17:42.646 --> 00:17:46.358
No. I don't want to see.
And I have to pick up Dara.

159
00:18:18.182 --> 00:18:20.434
Sam, you're late. Hurry up!

160
00:19:04.228 --> 00:19:06.688
Okay, put your hands together.
Let's pray.

161
00:19:52.109 --> 00:19:53.569
Stay away.

162
00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:38.071
I'm changing my bet.
50,000 on Sathian.

163
00:22:29.725 --> 00:22:31.101
For the next three matches.

164
00:22:31.894 --> 00:22:33.562
If you want more,
my door is open.

165
00:22:37.774 --> 00:22:39.693
You know I need the money.

166
00:22:45.616 --> 00:22:46.950
Look at his face.

167
00:22:47.117 --> 00:22:48.660
Your guy is on something.

168
00:22:49.661 --> 00:22:51.788
It's normal around here.
You know that.

169
00:22:51.997 --> 00:22:52.956
We agreed.

170
00:22:53.123 --> 00:22:56.293
Stay away from Sam's face.
Why is your guy doped?

171
00:22:56.668 --> 00:22:58.295
- You used to be.
- That was before.

172
00:22:58.504 --> 00:23:00.422
- Before you killed someone?
- Asshole.

173
00:23:00.672 --> 00:23:01.465
Hansa!

174
00:23:03.717 --> 00:23:04.426
Enough.

175
00:23:16.063 --> 00:23:18.190
Let's grab a beer at Paradise.

176
00:23:27.282 --> 00:23:29.284
{\an8}LAND FOR SALE

177
00:23:39.753 --> 00:23:40.295
Dara!

178
00:23:52.349 --> 00:23:52.933
See that bar?

179
00:23:53.392 --> 00:23:54.726
We'll keep it.

180
00:23:54.893 --> 00:23:57.187
But I have an even more amazing idea.

181
00:23:57.521 --> 00:24:00.566
A gigantic stage.
Look!

182
00:24:03.151 --> 00:24:04.361
It would go from here...

183
00:24:04.862 --> 00:24:05.988
all the way...

184
00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:09.783
to here!

185
00:24:10.742 --> 00:24:13.537
We'll put out cushions,
and do karaoke on Saturdays.

186
00:24:13.704 --> 00:24:16.290
And I'll host the rest of the week.

187
00:24:21.962 --> 00:24:22.629
First, our appointment.

188
00:24:23.213 --> 00:24:26.008
Then, we'll work on your theme parties.
Okay?

189
00:25:11.178 --> 00:25:12.679
Next, please.

190
00:25:20.812 --> 00:25:23.273
- First and last name.
- Mia Tanhtham.

191
00:25:23.482 --> 00:25:24.650
Are you really Thai?

192
00:25:24.816 --> 00:25:27.945
Yes, my father is Thai.
My mother is French.

193
00:25:31.615 --> 00:25:33.784
We're here for the property transfer.

194
00:25:36.537 --> 00:25:38.038
We can pay the remaining part in cash.

195
00:25:41.917 --> 00:25:43.710
When did you return to Thailand?

196
00:25:43.877 --> 00:25:46.213
7 years ago, when my daughter was born.

197
00:25:48.382 --> 00:25:49.508
Is he the father?

198
00:25:50.926 --> 00:25:52.719
The father stayed in France.

199
00:25:53.595 --> 00:25:55.138
We met here.

200
00:26:05.107 --> 00:26:07.276
Look at this <i>farang</i>, without papers!

201
00:26:07.442 --> 00:26:09.194
How do we know who he is?

202
00:26:09.361 --> 00:26:13.198
- Sorry, we're here for the property.
- I still have to check your papers.

203
00:26:49.401 --> 00:26:50.736
There's a problem.

204
00:26:51.278 --> 00:26:53.989
The owner isn't selling to you anymore.

205
00:26:54.156 --> 00:26:56.283
- What?
- I'm sorry.

206
00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:58.952
Someone made him a better offer.

207
00:26:59.578 --> 00:27:01.038
Next, please!

208
00:27:02.456 --> 00:27:05.292
- Shit! All they want is money!
- Mia, I don't understand.

209
00:27:05.626 --> 00:27:07.711
What did he say?
That we lost it?

210
00:27:07.878 --> 00:27:10.130
- Someone made a better offer.
- Don't worry.

211
00:27:11.423 --> 00:27:13.133
We'll just pay a little more.

212
00:27:13.300 --> 00:27:14.593
We've nothing left...

213
00:27:20.349 --> 00:27:22.309
Mia, it's no big deal.

214
00:28:05.060 --> 00:28:06.103
Be right with you.

215
00:28:19.199 --> 00:28:20.117
You okay?

216
00:28:21.034 --> 00:28:21.994
Yeah.

217
00:28:22.411 --> 00:28:23.537
Where is Sombat?

218
00:28:23.996 --> 00:28:25.622
Out on the terrace.

219
00:28:28.542 --> 00:28:29.918
You know him?

220
00:28:31.128 --> 00:28:32.129
Narong?

221
00:29:16.798 --> 00:29:17.966
See you there.

222
00:29:25.224 --> 00:29:26.475
How are you?

223
00:29:44.660 --> 00:29:46.286
Please, sit down!

224
00:29:51.208 --> 00:29:53.252
Sam, is that right?

225
00:29:54.086 --> 00:29:55.587
- You're French?
- I am.

226
00:29:55.754 --> 00:29:57.130
Nobody's perfect.

227
00:29:58.465 --> 00:30:01.134
Sombat tells me
you need a helping hand.

228
00:30:01.885 --> 00:30:04.930
We're trying to buy Noï's land
on the beach.

229
00:30:06.265 --> 00:30:08.475
I know it. Nice spot.

230
00:30:09.726 --> 00:30:11.270
Apparently, you outbid us.

231
00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:13.814
But...

232
00:30:14.940 --> 00:30:16.525
you want to buy the land...

233
00:30:16.900 --> 00:30:18.402
Do you have Thai citizenship?

234
00:30:19.278 --> 00:30:19.987
No.

235
00:30:20.737 --> 00:30:22.114
It'll be in my wife's name.

236
00:30:36.461 --> 00:30:37.462
Don't worry.

237
00:30:37.796 --> 00:30:40.966
You're not the first<i> farang
</i>to get fleeced by a pretty Thai girl.

238
00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:47.931
Hey, relax. We're just kidding.

239
00:30:48.515 --> 00:30:50.726
I'm sure your wife's not like that.

240
00:30:54.438 --> 00:30:57.691
Hey, I'm kidding.
Can't you take a joke?

241
00:30:59.860 --> 00:31:01.195
- Two noodle soups!

242
00:31:01.361 --> 00:31:03.322
- What?
- Two noodle soups!

243
00:31:03.864 --> 00:31:06.283
- More food?
- You heard us, old lady.

244
00:31:06.450 --> 00:31:08.202
Two soups and that's it!

245
00:31:09.119 --> 00:31:11.121
It's not like you're eating for free!

246
00:31:11.663 --> 00:31:13.040
Hurry! We're waiting!

247
00:31:16.460 --> 00:31:17.586
So...

248
00:31:17.920 --> 00:31:18.837
Listen,

249
00:31:19.838 --> 00:31:22.633
- We aren't rich but...
- Money, always money!

250
00:31:23.008 --> 00:31:25.677
Why do people always talk about money?

251
00:31:27.638 --> 00:31:28.597
Listen...

252
00:31:28.972 --> 00:31:30.724
You really want that land?

253
00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:36.188
I get it. I know what that's like.

254
00:31:38.398 --> 00:31:39.900
When I first got here,

255
00:31:40.067 --> 00:31:41.735
someone gave me a chance.

256
00:31:42.110 --> 00:31:45.072
I met a person who believed in me.
I did a few favors,

257
00:31:46.490 --> 00:31:47.783
and look at me today.

258
00:31:49.535 --> 00:31:51.995
I always knew that someday,
it would be my turn

259
00:31:52.454 --> 00:31:54.331
to give someone a chance.

260
00:31:55.958 --> 00:31:58.126
Sam, I want that person to be you.

261
00:32:00.504 --> 00:32:02.130
So, my question is...

262
00:32:03.423 --> 00:32:05.467
what can you do for me?

263
00:32:08.595 --> 00:32:10.222
You work at the airport, right?

264
00:32:11.348 --> 00:32:13.433
You have clearance and a pass.

265
00:32:15.686 --> 00:32:17.896
Move something for me,
and the land is yours.

266
00:32:19.439 --> 00:32:20.732
That's impossible.

267
00:32:21.900 --> 00:32:23.151
It's way too risky.

268
00:32:23.443 --> 00:32:26.738
I understand.
Then, it'll cost you 30,000 instead.

269
00:32:27.155 --> 00:32:27.865
How much?

270
00:32:28.198 --> 00:32:31.243
30,000 or no restaurant.
What can I say?

271
00:32:33.704 --> 00:32:35.038
Think it over.

272
00:32:35.539 --> 00:32:37.291
I'm not asking for much.

273
00:32:37.499 --> 00:32:40.335
Do it just once,
and that nice spot is yours.

274
00:32:42.629 --> 00:32:43.505
Sam,

275
00:32:44.339 --> 00:32:45.966
you and I are the same.

276
00:32:46.508 --> 00:32:48.844
We both deserve a second chance,
don't we?

277
00:32:49.553 --> 00:32:51.471
We didn't leave France for nothing,

278
00:32:53.682 --> 00:32:55.017
Samir Darba?

279
00:33:03.901 --> 00:33:05.360
Eat, it'll be cold.

280
00:33:58.163 --> 00:33:59.164
You okay?

281
00:34:50.047 --> 00:34:52.259
Damn, this is the middle of nowhere!

282
00:34:52.717 --> 00:34:54.594
I'm glad you came around.

283
00:34:55.679 --> 00:34:56.346
Kasem?

284
00:35:11.069 --> 00:35:13.530
Do what you always do.
Don't change anything.

285
00:35:13.780 --> 00:35:17.409
Follow Kim and leave the suitcase
where he tells you.

286
00:35:18.577 --> 00:35:20.329
I trust you, Sam.

287
00:35:22.623 --> 00:35:23.498
Okay, let's go.

288
00:35:57.032 --> 00:35:57.866
Hello.

289
00:35:58.033 --> 00:35:59.284
Your badge, please.

290
00:36:27.020 --> 00:36:27.855
Go ahead.

291
00:37:56.902 --> 00:37:58.529
Stop. Badge, please.

292
00:38:45.868 --> 00:38:47.578
Stop !

293
00:40:59.751 --> 00:41:01.003
Dara, wake up.

294
00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:02.546
Mia!

295
00:41:02.713 --> 00:41:04.756
- We're leaving.
- What's going on?

296
00:41:04.923 --> 00:41:06.175
I can't explain now!

297
00:41:06.842 --> 00:41:07.801
Come, honey.

298
00:41:07.968 --> 00:41:09.136
Sam, explain to me!

299
00:41:09.595 --> 00:41:10.512
We have to go!

300
00:41:10.679 --> 00:41:12.014
- Explain!
- I will!

301
00:41:18.562 --> 00:41:20.522
Take Dara into the room.
Now!

302
00:41:46.673 --> 00:41:47.174
Run!

303
00:41:51.845 --> 00:41:53.138
Come here!

304
00:41:53.722 --> 00:41:55.140
Let her go!

305
00:42:03.106 --> 00:42:04.483
Shut her up!

306
00:42:05.484 --> 00:42:06.693
Kasem, let's go!

307
00:43:47.503 --> 00:43:48.462
Time to go.

308
00:44:29.795 --> 00:44:31.213
Goodbye, Samir Darba.

309
00:49:22.921 --> 00:49:23.839
Did you eat?

310
00:53:30.919 --> 00:53:32.462
- I don't know.
- Narong.

311
00:53:32.629 --> 00:53:34.590
- I don't know him. Noï!
- Yes, mum?

312
00:53:35.174 --> 00:53:36.466
- Hey, come on and eat some noodles!

313
00:53:40.762 --> 00:53:42.139
- I don't know him.

314
00:53:51.398 --> 00:53:53.066
That bastard Kasem.

315
00:54:01.575 --> 00:54:02.743
Search in town.

316
00:54:27.768 --> 00:54:28.644
Do you know Kasem?

317
00:54:29.686 --> 00:54:31.522
Where are the Lady Boys bars?

318
00:54:44.576 --> 00:54:46.119
- Do you know Kasem?
- No.

319
00:55:01.844 --> 00:55:03.345
Do you know Kasem?

320
00:55:18.944 --> 00:55:20.320
Where can he find him?

321
00:55:35.836 --> 00:55:37.754
He loves playing the lord...

322
01:00:07.149 --> 01:00:09.318
You can do anything you want
with her.

323
01:00:09.484 --> 01:00:11.862
- What about these four?
- Later...

324
01:00:33.842 --> 01:00:34.968
What's wrong with you?

325
01:01:55.716 --> 01:01:56.884
Wait!

326
01:01:57.384 --> 01:01:58.552
Your daughter is alive!

327
01:02:21.200 --> 01:02:22.034
I'm a guest!

328
01:02:22.451 --> 01:02:23.327
I'm a guest!

329
01:02:43.722 --> 01:02:46.517
We often see little girls,
but they're not here.

330
01:02:46.850 --> 01:02:49.520
They're sent to Bangkok to work.

331
01:02:51.271 --> 01:02:52.314
They vanish!

332
01:04:09.975 --> 01:04:11.059
Dara is not dead!

333
01:10:33.150 --> 01:10:33.984
Mother?

334
01:10:41.074 --> 01:10:41.950
Get back to work.

335
01:12:46.533 --> 01:12:47.409
Where is he?

336
01:15:45.420 --> 01:15:46.380
Have you seen her?

337
01:18:05.352 --> 01:18:06.603
Please, no!

338
01:18:13.360 --> 01:18:14.778
Don't be scared.

339
01:18:24.621 --> 01:18:26.623
Some children arrived two weeks ago.

340
01:18:26.999 --> 01:18:28.959
But they were taken away yesterday.

341
01:18:57.196 --> 01:18:57.988
Out! Hurry!

342
01:25:10.903 --> 01:25:12.696
Look at the state you're in.

343
01:25:15.032 --> 01:25:15.908
Proud of yourself?

344
01:25:22.998 --> 01:25:23.916
My daughter...

345
01:25:24.875 --> 01:25:26.585
Your daughter...
You're a pain in my ass.

346
01:25:26.752 --> 01:25:28.420
Look at the mess you've made.

347
01:25:41.016 --> 01:25:42.518
Everything was so easy though.

348
01:25:50.817 --> 01:25:51.902
We were after you.

349
01:25:55.572 --> 01:25:57.115
Yes, Samir.
Small world.

350
01:25:58.075 --> 01:26:00.285
Farhat never got over
his brother's death.

351
01:26:01.203 --> 01:26:02.287
Remember that?

352
01:26:11.463 --> 01:26:13.966
For five years,
Farhat had Kasem hunt you down.

353
01:26:20.305 --> 01:26:23.225
It was pretty easy
to get Sombat to give you up.

354
01:26:25.185 --> 01:26:26.436
He's a real piece of shit.

355
01:26:37.030 --> 01:26:39.241
My daughter!

356
01:26:45.747 --> 01:26:46.832
Your daughter?

357
01:26:48.292 --> 01:26:50.169
The kid never left Bang Chan.

358
01:27:03.098 --> 01:27:04.183
What a shame.

359
01:27:06.268 --> 01:27:08.145
Look what you're making me do.

360
01:29:45.677 --> 01:29:47.012
Hurry, children. Faster.

361
01:33:39.786 --> 01:33:40.704
<i>Daddy!</i>

362
01:33:58.847 --> 01:33:59.890
Daddy!

363
01:34:17.741 --> 01:34:19.076
Where were you, Daddy?

364
01:34:21.828 --> 01:34:23.956
I missed you, Daddy!

365
01:34:27.501 --> 01:34:30.003
I thought you were dead!
